{"abstract":"This paper critically examines the machine learning (ML) modeling of humans in three case studies of well-being technologies. Through a critical technical approach, it examines how these apps were experienced in daily life (technology in use) to surface breakdowns and to identify the assumptions about the “human” body entrenched in the ML models (technology design). To address these issues, this paper applies agential realism to decenter foundational assumptions, such as body regularity and health/illness binaries, and speculates more inclusive design and ML modeling paths that acknowledge irregularity, human-system entanglements, and uncertain transitions. This work is among the first to explore the implications of decentering theories in computational modeling of human bodies and well-being, offering insights for more inclusive technologies and speculations toward posthuman-centered ML modeling.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhu, Jichen","Sanches, Pedro","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","van der Maden, Willem","Kaklopoulou, Irene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808913"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Agential realism","Decentering","Diffraction","Well being"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the centers and margins of modeling humans in well being technologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3706598.3713940","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808913","identifier":[{"id":"105005712509","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6340b37e-db29-4950-99d9-e79c2f96d4a4"],"keyword":["Agential Realism","Decentering","Diffraction","Machine Learning Modeling","Well-being"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2699132873982139CD21194131A7BEB7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3706598.3713940","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Willem","key":"vandermadenpau","last":"van der Maden","locid":"1ee9fda3-cb4e-4c06-82b1-7e248c20a700","name":"van der Maden, Willem","orcid":"0000-0003-0245-1633","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"kaklopouloupau","last":"Kaklopoulou","name":"Kaklopoulou, Irene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3706598.3713940","eisbn":["9798400713941"],"pages":"1-16","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2025 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005712509"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6340b37e-db29-4950-99d9-e79c2f96d4a4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Centers and Margins of Modeling Humans in Well-being Technologies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808913","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents three scenario-based speculations accompanied by material explorations of soft IoT for smart homes based on humidity data. Cycle Lines tracks and displays weekly patterns of humidity levels shown as colored lines in a woven display, Relationscape, a real-time tracker and knitted display of humidity showing the relation between two different households, and Eco-collective, embroidery IoT that changes color depending on the humidity levels of different objects in the household. Based on first-person engagements with humidity sensors placed in the authors’ homes, they imagine new types of soft IoT devices that sense and display relations to humidity data, suggesting a role for mundane,craft-based IoT for smart homes. They express the relational nature of humidity and how it is tied to well-being in the home, among household members and other human and more-than-human inhabitants, as well as the environmental conditions inside and outside of the home. The soft, craft-based approach to imagining futures of IoT for smart homes has feminist commitments and invites for further problematizing domestic labor practices and craft activism in the domestic context.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Jørgensen, Stina Marie Hasse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828145"],"event":{"acronym":"Nordes","title":"Nordic Design Research Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Craft","Scenarios","Smart home"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imagining a soft and relational smart home","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/112678447/Imagining_a_Soft_and_Relational_Smart_Home.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828145","ids":["itu-36f98c62-1269-42c1-bc20-0df2bc889ef5"],"keyword":["Craft","Humidity data","Scenarios","Smart Home","Soft IoT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-335DF05C2942634B94B1A3D4D15AF7B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/112678447/Imagining_a_Soft_and_Relational_Smart_Home.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Marie Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Marie Hasse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","title":"Nordic Design Research Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36f98c62-1269-42c1-bc20-0df2bc889ef5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Imagining a Soft and Relational Smart Home","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828145","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Several researchers have been studying how working with materials such as yarn can shift how we think and theorize relations to the body and others, by bringing together feminist values at the intersection of data, technology, and hands-on making. Extending such prior work, our research, anchored in craft-based knowledge production, aims to contribute with explorations on knotting as a feminist approach to data materialization. We present a year-long process consisting of 4 workshops we conducted with participants, in which we used differ-ent forms of knotting to materialize data about bodies being part of our academic institution and the Covid-19 pandemic. Presenting the workshops and their outcomes, we discuss how knotting as an approach to materializing data can: 1. put a focus on missing data, 2. surface corporeal and affective vulnerabilities, 3. contribute to making new relations with other (non-human) bodies, and 4. trouble notions of time.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Tatjana Reime, Lara","Cohn, Marisa","Pérez-Bustos, Tania"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754067"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"country":["Colombia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National University of Colombia"],"keyword":["Body","Crafts","Data","Feminism","Materialization","khipu","knotting","macramé"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"knotting data as a feminist approach to data materialization","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.879","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754067","ids":["itu-242c5614-07a9-4745-a8ef-0a07a28ab52a"],"keyword":["body","crafts","data","feminism","khipu","knotting","macramé","materialization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5951EB1867AF2EEE8CE809DD532780C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.designresearchsociety.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=3405&context=drs-conference-papers","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.designresearchsociety.org/drs-conference-papers/drs2024/researchpapers/270/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.879","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"co","key":"national university of colombia","loc":["Colombia","America, South","OECD"],"name":"National University of Colombia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lara","key":"reimepau","last":"Reime","locid":"0baaf9f8-3126-4cb1-b22f-b9fceabb8b54","name":"Tatjana Reime, Lara","name_org":"Reime, Lara","orcid":"0000-0002-7475-2147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tania","key":"pérezbustospau","last":"Pérez-Bustos","name":"Pérez-Bustos, Tania","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2024.879","status":"p","title":"DRS2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-242c5614-07a9-4745-a8ef-0a07a28ab52a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Knotting data as a feminist approach to data materialization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754067","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This one-day workshop seeks to bring together design researchers that have different orientations and practices for futures and futur- ing to unpack the role of futuring across design, design artefacts, and designers. Our goal in this workshop is to use examples of established futures to engage with and reflect on questions around the role of futures in HCI/design. We believe that there is a common thread between work from many different researchers, but that the people doing that work are spread across different disciplines and geographical locations. To that end, this workshop will assem- ble researchers working with different methods and approaches to futures in design and will aim to identify core challenges and opportunities for futures in HCI.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Boer, Laurens","Kun, Peter","Howell, Noura","Wong, Richmond","Campo Woytuk, Nadia","Søndergaard, Maria Louise Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759409"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Design Futuring","Design research","Futures"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mapping futures and futuring in hci design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/%2010.1145/3656156.3658384","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759409","identifier":[{"id":"85198906038","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-91abe117-12cd-4c3b-9943-34ab75c4ac66"],"keyword":["design futuring","design research","futures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E149DA731F91BC1D38C3C0F1DE88B83"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105488248/2024_Jenkins_et_al_-_Mapping_Futures_and_Futuring_in_HCI_Design.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/%2010.1145/3656156.3658384","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"aho the oslo school of architecture and design norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","locid":"f30d35c6-4320-476f-8506-481764e6009e","name":"Kun, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0778-7662","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Noura","key":"howellpau","last":"Howell","name":"Howell, Noura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richmond","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Richmond","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"campowoytukpau","last":"Campo Woytuk","name":"Campo Woytuk, Nadia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Louise Juul","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Maria Louise Juul","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3658384","pages":"458-461","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Designing Interactive Systems Conference 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198906038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-91abe117-12cd-4c3b-9943-34ab75c4ac66"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mapping Futures and Futuring in HCI/Design","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759409","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Reproductive technologies encompass aspects of menstrual health, in/fertility, sexual health, pregnancy, contraception, abortion, or menopause, among many other things, thus entangling aspects of the everyday lives of people of all genders. As reproductive technologies have become-and will continue to be-complicit in enabling or challenging the oppressions enacted on our bodies, it is imperative that we critically reflect on the values and methods used when designing these technologies. Despite a growing body of critical work in HCI, we, a community of feminist scholars working on reproductive technologies, find that there is limited practical guidance on bringing together perspectives such that they can be distributed in easy-to-use, engaging, and collaborative ways. This critical visualization responds to these needs and presents a zine (a collaboratively made booklet) that speculates on reproductive technologies by providing examples from a previous design workshop that happened at NordiCHI 2022 and a guide with activities and reflections on how to organize this kind of workshop. We have also included instructions on how to print and assemble the zine. Some of the examples featured in the zine imagine utopian feminist futures, and some of them intentionally expose or 'trouble' the taken-for-granted dichotomies behind the design and use of reproductive technologies. For instance, several examples draw from the feminist value of embodiment and prioritize the qualitative and felt experiences of menstruating. Other projects highlight the risks of reproductive bodies being commodified and surveilled through technology. The projects are presented through a lens of 'feminist values', which are particularly useful for critically highlighting existing power structures and instead centering subjective experiences that are typically erased in (cis-)normative approaches to reproductive health. We intend the zine to act as a collaborative, accessible, low-tech, and open-ended feminist tool and to use it as a stepping-stone for bringing together an already flourishing community of designers and researchers. Since the zine itself allows for reassembling and reconfiguring, we envision an impromptu zine-assembling activity at the conference presentation, where we invite the audience to add their own feminist values and experiences of designing (and using) reproductive technologies. The zine is free and accessible online, ready to be used in future workshops, offering it as a guide, but also as an easy way to get acquainted with feminist vocabulary in general. We hope this work is one step towards formalizing an (open) community of people working with designing and researching reproductive technologies in the Nordics.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Campo Woytuk, Nadia","Park, Joo Young","Reime, Lara","Søndergaard, Marie Louise Juul","Yadav, Deepika","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Homewood, Sarah","Gamboa, Mafalda"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811217"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Institute of Design, The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a zine for feminist design of reproductive technologies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-811217","ids":["ku-db93485c-2eda-47fa-ad28-f9299c28c27b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3CC4A55A1664BCFF0AE8328202D85772"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institute of Design, The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nadia","key":"campowoytukpau","last":"Campo Woytuk","name":"Campo Woytuk, Nadia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joo Young","key":"parkpau","last":"Park","name":"Park, Joo Young","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lara","key":"reimepau","last":"Reime","name":"Reime, Lara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Marie Louise Juul","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Marie Louise Juul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Deepika","key":"yadavpau","last":"Yadav","name":"Yadav, Deepika","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","locid":"e6edf1cc-cfc0-4304-8638-989154e536d8","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mafalda","key":"gamboapau","last":"Gamboa","name":"Gamboa, Mafalda","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685497","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '24 Adjunct: Adjunct Proceedings of the 2024 Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-db93485c-2eda-47fa-ad28-f9299c28c27b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Zine for Feminist Design of Reproductive Technologies","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811217","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Through close analysis of fertility and menstrual cycle tracking apps, this contribution explores how reproductive bodies, and their temporalities are understood, made and reshaped with and through technologies. We rethink reproductive temporalities through the lens of Kafer’s (2013) and Forlano’s (2017) notion of queer/crip time to account for the different and individual temporalities of bodies. By tuning into the everyday rituals and temporalities that emerge when living with real-time data around sociocultural norms of reproduction (Forlano, 2017), we make visible how fertile bodies are in a constant state of becoming. Empirically, we home in on the processes of becoming or unbecoming fertile and engagements of self-tracking as well as practices of self-care by drawing on data inquired through digital ethnographic methods. To contextualize the analysis within broader, (sub-)cultural imaginaries of reproductive futures, we combine walkthroughs of apps (Light et al., 2018) with analysis of discussions and data-sharing practices on social network sites dedicated to fertility tracking and queer/non-binary experiences of reproduction.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tatjana Reime, Lara","Cohn, Marisa","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718936"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital ethnography","Fertility tracking apps","Queer crip time","Reproductive temporalities","Self tracking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fertile becoming reproductive temporalities with in tracking technologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102855001/pre-print_fertile_becoming_2023.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-718936","identifier":[{"id":"85198247032","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fbd3ff6a-908d-4997-a8e8-45223b55cc14"],"keyword":["Digital ethnography","Fertility tracking apps","Queer/crip time","Reproductive temporalities","Self-tracking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AAABD1397F3CD55C3DB130BA255A8C0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102855001/pre-print_fertile_becoming_2023.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lara","key":"tatjanareimepau","last":"Tatjana Reime","locid":"0baaf9f8-3126-4cb1-b22f-b9fceabb8b54","name":"Tatjana Reime, Lara","orcid":"0000-0002-7475-2147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lindsay","key":"balfourpedh","last":"Balfour","name":"Balfour, Lindsay","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789819956050"],"pages":"73-97","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"FemTech: Intersectional Interventions in Women’s Digital Health"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198247032"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fbd3ff6a-908d-4997-a8e8-45223b55cc14"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fertile Becoming: Reproductive Temporalities with/in Tracking Technologies","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718936","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This one-day workshop will explore fabulations in design research. Bringing together design researchers and practitioners in hands-on exploration and critical dialogue, we will explore emerging practices and potentials of using fabulations in futures-oriented and exploratory practice-based design research. Drawing on fabulations’ relations with feminist technoscience and more-than-human concerns, we seek to understand if and how the practice of fabulating can contribute to designing vibrant worlds that can flourish in new ways.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","Sanches, Pedro","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Campo Woytuk, Nadia","Howell, Noura","Helms, Karey","Boer, Laurens","Tucker, Jason"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718887"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Malmö University","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Design research","Fabulations","Feminist Technoscience","More than Human Concerns","Practice Based Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fabulating futures for flourishing and vibrant worlds","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100699342/177_submission.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718887","ids":["itu-8c307203-7f4e-4edc-8514-f3cf70b8c2cd"],"keyword":["Design Research","Fabulations","Feminist Technoscience","More-than-Human Concerns","Practice-based Research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BF7D4A13C4B1615C441B35456274B19B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100699342/177_submission.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"aho the oslo school of architecture and design norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise","key":"juulsøndergaardpau","last":"Juul Søndergaard","name":"Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia","key":"campowoytukpau","last":"Campo Woytuk","name":"Campo Woytuk, Nadia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Noura","key":"howellpau","last":"Howell","name":"Howell, Noura","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Karey","key":"helmspau","last":"Helms","name":"Helms, Karey","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason","key":"tuckerpau","last":"Tucker","name":"Tucker, Jason","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","title":"The 10th Nordic Design Research Society (Nordes) Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8c307203-7f4e-4edc-8514-f3cf70b8c2cd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fabulating Futures for Flourishing and Vibrant Worlds","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718887","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Menstruation and fertility tracking applications are of increasing concern in HCI research, as their use becomes more widespread. Methods are needed to understand how such applications become entangled in everyday practices. While these apps promise increased self-knowledge of reproductive potential by collecting intimate data about reproductive bodies, they also restrict the knowledge produced about users’ bodies and embed normative understandings of reproduction and gender. In this paper, we scrutinize the normativities of reproductive bodies by deploying the “walkthrough method” to uncover sociotechnical entanglements of the menstruation and fertility apps Clue, Tilly, and Drip. We discuss how the walkthrough method contributes to HCI's methodological repertoire for studying intimate bodily tracking apps and unpacking their normativities. We offer suggestions for using this method to critically analyze existing apps and extend approaches to design with and for a plurality of in/fertile bodies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tatjana Reime, Lara","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Cohn, Marisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677319"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fertility apps","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Intimate data collection","Menstruation tracking","Normative understandings","Plurality in design","Reproductive bodies","Reproductive health","Sociotechnical entanglements","Walkthrough method"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"walking through normativities of reproductive bodies a method for critical analysis of tracking applications","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544548.3581450","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677319","identifier":[{"id":"85160005909","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-716354a2-2bc8-4489-b1fa-4724ba37117b"],"keyword":["Fertility apps","Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)","Intimate data collection","Menstruation tracking","Normative understandings","Plurality in design","Reproductive bodies","Reproductive health","Sociotechnical entanglements","Walkthrough method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-689E547FB404D5B32E97D56A9150B675"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544548.3581450","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lara","key":"tatjanareimepau","last":"Tatjana Reime","locid":"0baaf9f8-3126-4cb1-b22f-b9fceabb8b54","name":"Tatjana Reime, Lara","orcid":"0000-0002-7475-2147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3544548.3581450","eisbn":["9781450394215"],"pages":"1-15","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","stat