, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/nordes.2023.47","publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","title":"Nordes 2023: This Space Intentionally Left Blank, 12-14 June, Linköping University, Norrköping, Sweden"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9cc9d2fc-4b52-45de-be3e-3ee489da1338"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Craft as a matter of care to inspire the design of computational things","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718898","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present breathing-with as a contribution to cultivating concrete design tactics engaging with the more-than-human. We arrive at the concept based on an analysis of three distinct projects, each aimed at exploring the relationality between human and non-human bodies, and of extending the notion of the body in design processes toward the more-than-human, with a focus on breath and breathing. We analyze each project from the perspective of how breathing allowed us as designers to move from the intimate experience of our own bodies into an extended bodily awareness that included the more-than-human as material, living and social bodies. Based on this exploration, we propose breathing-with as a design tactic that can be used throughout the design process. We further reflect on how breathing-with can provide a generative design tactic for zooming in and out of the entangled relationships between human and more-than-human bodies, through surfacing notions of intimacy and vulnerability.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Ryding, Karin","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718845"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Breathing","Intimacy","More than human","Posthuman","Soma Design","Vulnerability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"breathing with a design tactic for the more than human","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102396410/Breathing_with_Design_Tactic_for_the_More_than_Human_FINAL.docx","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718845","identifier":[{"id":"85177567387","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-429d4005-4f94-484b-bbbc-fce96f5eb703"],"keyword":["affective interaction design","breathing","intimacy","more-than-human","posthuman","soma design","vulnerability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-91DA7F20BF7D5110D462BD1BD86D7EB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102396410/Breathing_with_Design_Tactic_for_the_More_than_Human_FINAL.docx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"rydingpau","last":"Ryding","name":"Ryding, Karin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/07370024.2023.2275760","issn":["07370024","15327051"],"issn_org":["07370024"],"journal":"Human-Computer Interaction","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177567387"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-429d4005-4f94-484b-bbbc-fce96f5eb703"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘Breathing-with’: a Design Tactic for the More-than Human","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718845","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Envisioning alternative futures and desirable worlds is a core element of design that must be cultivated, especially when a deep transition of practices, values, and power is necessary for vibrant and just future lifeworlds. In this paper, we contribute towards fabulation as an approach for design futuring that foregrounds feminist commitments and more-than-human concerns. Analyzing two fabulation case studies around biodata and bodily fluids, we offer three themes based on our process of developing these fabulations: how they engage materials, how they work to trouble temporalities, and how they cultivate imagination. We argue for the emerging potential of fabulation as an approach for open-ended, joyful design futuring, mobilizing speculative storytelling to foreground absent or neglected relations when imagining alternative lifeworlds.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","Campo Woytuk, Nadia","Howell, Noura","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Helms, Karey","Jenkins, Tom","Sanches, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718921"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Critical Feminist Technoscience","Design Futuring","Fabulation","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fabulation as an approach for design futuring","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700021/2023_S_ndergaard_et_al_Fabulation_as_an_Approach_for_Design_Futuring.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718921","ids":["itu-d2cdd24b-1c04-4094-a8e7-1c480e885a51"],"keyword":["Critical Feminist Technoscience","Design Futuring","Fabulation","Research through Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-59CB0325CF8664E9CEDF12EC8223DDEA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700021/2023_S_ndergaard_et_al_Fabulation_as_an_Approach_for_Design_Futuring.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3563657.3596097","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"aho the oslo school of architecture and design norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT Univer