{"abstract":"In this paper, we reflect on the applicability of the concept of trajectories to soma design. Soma design is a first-person design method which considers users’ subjective somatic or bodily experiences of a design. Due to bodily changes over time, soma experiences are inherently temporal. Current instruments for articulating soma experiences lack the power to express the effects of experiences on the body over time. To address this, we turn to trajectories, a well-known concept in the HCI community, as a way of mapping this aspect of soma experience. By showing trajectories through a range of dimensions, we can articulate individual experiences and differences in those experiences. Through analysis of a set of soma experience designs and a set of temporal dimensions within the experiences, this paper demonstrates how trajectories can provide a practical conceptual framing for articulating the temporal complexity of soma designs.","author_count":14,"contributors":["TENNENT, PAUL","HÖÖK, KRISTINA","BENFORD, STEVE","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","STÅHL, ANNA","DAUDÉN ROQUET, CLAUDIA","WINDLIN, CHARLES","SANCHES, PEDRO","MARSHALL, JOSEPH","LI, CHRISTINE","MARTINEZ AVILA, JUAN","ALFARAS, MIQUEL","UMAIR, MUHAMMAD","ZHOU, FENG"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383164"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Lancaster University","SICS RISE","UNIVERSITAT JAUME I","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Bodily experience","Human Computer Interaction","Soma Design","Temporal Experiences","Trajectories"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"articulating soma experiences using trajectories","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86265697/Soma_Trajectories_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383164","identifier":[{"id":"85106710030","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-814405e4-6eb8-480c-98de-06acf194c07d"],"keyword":["Bodily Experience","Human-Computer Interaction","Soma Design","Temporal Experiences","Trajectories"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-853AC537C195FCDF76838CB2C3EA3CD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86265697/Soma_Trajectories_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"sics rise","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SICS RISE","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"lancaster university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lancaster University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"es","key":"universitat jaume i","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UNIVERSITAT JAUME I","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"PAUL","key":"tennentpau","last":"TENNENT","name":"TENNENT, PAUL","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"KRISTINA","key":"höökpau","last":"HÖÖK","name":"HÖÖK, KRISTINA","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"STEVE","key":"benfordpau","last":"BENFORD","name":"BENFORD, STEVE","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"ANNA","key":"ståhlpau","last":"STÅHL","name":"STÅHL, ANNA","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"CLAUDIA","key":"daudénroquetpau","last":"DAUDÉN ROQUET","name":"DAUDÉN ROQUET, CLAUDIA","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"CHARLES","key":"windlinpau","last":"WINDLIN","name":"WINDLIN, CHARLES","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"PEDRO","key":"sanchespau","last":"SANCHES","name":"SANCHES, PEDRO","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"JOSEPH","key":"marshallpau","last":"MARSHALL","name":"MARSHALL, JOSEPH","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"CHRISTINE","key":"lipau","last":"LI","name":"LI, CHRISTINE","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"JUAN","key":"martinezavilapau","last":"MARTINEZ AVILA","name":"MARTINEZ AVILA, JUAN","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"MIQUEL","key":"alfaraspau","last":"ALFARAS","name":"ALFARAS, MIQUEL","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"MUHAMMAD","key":"umairpau","last":"UMAIR","name":"UMAIR, MUHAMMAD","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"FENG","key":"zhoupau","last":"ZHOU","name":"ZHOU, FENG","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3411764.3445482","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2021 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-814405e4-6eb8-480c-98de-06acf194c07d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Articulating Soma Experiences using Trajectories","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383164","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"As new materials become available for textile and interaction designers, it is crucial that we develop an understanding of the lived experiences of such materials and explore meaningful contexts for their development. In this paper, we engage with systems in which bodies as materials and materials as bodies constitute an assemblage of vitalities in constant flux with one another. In particular, we address how such systems in their interactions with (non)human bodies blur boundaries between inside and outside the body, and between human and machine, acting as soft systems. Drawing on our first-person, design-led research, we present three design explorations of soft systems that deeply engage with the body: Breathing Wings, Fiddling Necklaces and Menarche Bits. We analyze how the three projects contribute towards what we conceptualize as “vibrant wearables”: wearables that through their material vibrancy surface design qualities of leakiness, characterized by a multi-directionality of “spilling over,” ongoingness, which attends to non-linear temporalities and cycles of life and death, and mutuality that emphasizes the interdependency, and becoming, of vibrant encounters. These three design qualities all conceptually trouble boundaries of bodies and materials and are practical resources for designers and researchers working with the body in/as a soft system. Our work offers concrete examples of how to work with material vibrancy, which is particularly relevant to new materialist discourses in textile, fashion and interaction design. We argue for the generativity of these design qualities for other designers and researchers aiming to elevate materials and soft systems in interactions with bodies. Moreover, we contribute towards design research that conceptually and materially troubles the boundaries of the body, and we argue for attending to the material power of (non)human bodies as a soft system.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Helms, Karey","Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","Ciolfi Felice, Marianela"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384276"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Body","Soft systems","Soma Design","Wearables","vibrant matte"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vibrant wearables material encounters with the body as a soft system","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/20511787.2021.1923202","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384276","ids":["itu-cd8f7db2-48b6-472a-be5c-c2df1477c8c8"],"keyword":["Soft systems","body","soma design","vibrant matte","wearables"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-908FC261CD05A30F066FBB2952EDA39A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86429746/vibrant_wearables_2021_accepted_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/20511787.2021.1923202","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"aho the oslo school of architecture and design norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AHO The Oslo School of Architecture and Design, Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karey","key":"helmspau","last":"Helms","name":"Helms, Karey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise","key":"juulsøndergaardpau","last":"Juul Søndergaard","name":"Juul Søndergaard, Marie Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianela","key":"ciolfifelicepau","last":"Ciolfi Felice","name":"Ciolfi Felice, Marianela","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/20511787.2021.1923202","issn":["20511787"],"issn_org":["20511795"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Textile Design Research and Practice","pages":"142-163","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Journal of Textile Design Research and Practice","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cd8f7db2-48b6-472a-be5c-c2df1477c8c8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“Vibrant Wearables”: Material Encounters with the Body as a Soft System","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384276","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We report on the design processes of two ongoing soma design projects: the Pelvic Chair and the Breathing Wings. These projects take a first-person, soma design approach, grounded in a holistic perspective of the mind and body (the soma). We contribute a reflective account of our soma design processes that deepens the field’s understanding of how soma design is achieved through first-person approaches. We show how we use our somas, our first-person experiences, to stimulate a design process, to prototype through and to use as a way of critiquing emerging designs. Grounding our analysis in new materialism, we show how our designs are in essence, “performative intra-actions”. Using our own somas, our designs open up for experiences within certain constraints, allowing for a material-discursive agency of sorts. Many different somas may be intra-acted through our designs, even if it was our somas who started them.","author_count":3,"contributors":["STÅHL, ANNA","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Balaam, Madeline"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383251"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","SICS RISE"],"keyword":["Design critique","Design methods","Feminism","New materialism","Sketching","Soma Design","first person perspectives"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validity and rigour in soma design sketching with the soma","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3470132","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383251","identifier":[{"id":"85122474673","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-874fdd75-8186-4dfc-8773-c0f4de6921b6"],"keyword":["design critique","design methods","feminism","first-person perspectives","new materialism","sketching","soma design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-37368136934EBECC828D1ABB7795A3A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3470132","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86447236/First_Person_Perspectives_in_Soma_Design_Sketching_with_the_Soma_1_.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"sics rise","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SICS RISE","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"ANNA","key":"ståhlpau","last":"STÅHL","name":"STÅHL, ANNA","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Madeline","key":"balaampau","last":"Balaam","name":"Balaam, Madeline","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3470132","issn":["10730516","15577325"],"issn_org":["10730516"],"journal":"ACM Transactions on Computer-Human Interaction","pages":"1-36","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Computer-Human Interaction","title_org":"A C M Transactions on Computer - Human Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122474673"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-874fdd75-8186-4dfc-8773-c0f4de6921b6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Validity and Rigour in Soma Design-Sketching with the Soma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383251","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We report on a somaesthetic design workshop and the subsequent analytical work aiming to demystify what is entailed in a non-dualistic design stance on embodied interaction and why a first-person engagement is crucial to its unfoldings. However, as we will uncover through a detailed account of our process, these first-person engagements are deeply entangled with second- and third-person perspectives, sometimes even overlapping. The analysis furthermore reveals some strategies for bridging the body-mind divide by attending to our inner universe and dissolving or traversing dichotomies between inside and outside; individual and social; body and technology. By detailing the creative process, we show how soma design becomes a process of designing with and through kinesthetic experience, in turn letting u","author_count":14,"contributors":["Höök, Kristina","BENFORD, STEVE","TENNENT, PAUL","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","ALFARAS, MIQUEL","MARTINEZ AVILA, JUAN","Li, Christine","Marshal, joseph","DAUDÉN ROQUET, CLAUDIA","SANCHES, PEDRO","STÅHL, ANNA","UMAIR, MUHAMMAD","WINDLIN, CHARLES","ZHOU, FENG"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383528"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Portugal","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ITI/LARSyS, ARDITI","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Lancaster University","SICS RISE","Stockholm University","UNIVERSITAT JAUME I","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Soma Design","Somaesthetics","first person"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unpacking non dualistic design the soma design case","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3462448","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383528","identifier":[{"id":"85122449400","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9aa19829-cc11-45fd-b4ed-7c6102e36ca4"],"keyword":["first person","soma design","somaesthetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E12CD4161220D1D5C3744C5E618EC1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86429962/Soma_Dimensions_in_Design_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3462448","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"universitat jaume i","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UNIVERSITAT JAUME I","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"lancaster university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lancaster University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"pt","key":"iti larsys arditi","l