{"abstract":"Movement plays an increasingly important role in interactive systems design, from users’ physical engagement, to how designed artefacts can move or be moved, and to the concert between users and artefacts. Designers, as well as programmers, have to engage more and more in physical activities when they want to create appealing experiences involving movement. There is a need for articulating emerging dialogues between designers, developers, and their materials. We will explore such dialogues in a 2-half-day workshop, focusing on data and its challenges, on tools and methods, on sensing and actuation when designing or detecting subtle body movements, and on catering for bodily changes over time.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bogdan, Cristian","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Windlin, Charles","Kilic Afsar, Ozgun","Eriksson, Sara","Fernaeus, Ylva","Sanches, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382274"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Body Material Interaction","Design Methodologies","Interactive systems design","Movement Sensing","Physical Engagement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"programming for moving bodies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3290605.3300847","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382274","identifier":[{"id":"85095826474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-43e75afc-3963-4b7f-b56e-4ae9f21a0c85"],"keyword":["Body-Material Interaction","Design Methodologies","Interactive Systems Design","Movement Sensing","Physical Engagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ADE4222F4CAD28D8BC1E9CC9920BD51E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85526555/3419249.3420069.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3290605.3300847","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cristian","key":"bogdanpau","last":"Bogdan","name":"Bogdan, Cristian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles","key":"windlinpau","last":"Windlin","name":"Windlin, Charles","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ozgun","key":"kilicafsarpau","last":"Kilic Afsar","name":"Kilic Afsar, Ozgun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Sara","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ylva","key":"fernaeuspau","last":"Fernaeus","name":"Fernaeus, Ylva","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3290605.3300847","pages":"1-12","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-43e75afc-3963-4b7f-b56e-4ae9f21a0c85"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Programming for Moving Bodies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382274","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"A diverse set of research and design initiatives related to time, temporality, and slowness has emerged in the DIS and HCI communities. The goals of this workshop are to: 1. bring together researchers to reflect on conceptual, methodological, and practice-based outcomes and issues and 2. to develop an agenda for future research in this growing area.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Odom, William","Lindley, Siân","Pschetz, Larissa","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Vallgårda, Anna","Wiberg, Mikael","Yoo, Daisy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382575"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Microsoft Research Cambridge","Simon Fraser University","Stockholm University","Umeå University","University of Edinburgh","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Slow Technology","Slowness","Temporality","Time"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"time temporality and slowness future directions for design research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83744920/p383_odom.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382575","identifier":[{"id":"85054165544","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-581cc703-541f-48fe-bcab-f47c1fb4c886"],"keyword":["Slow Technology","Slowness","Temporality","Time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D837550E4CF26987008CBD8768D0B3A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","t