{"abstract":"We propose the notion of material programming as a new practice for designing future interactive artifacts. Material programming would be a way for the interaction designer to better explore the dynamics of the materials at hand and through that familiarity be able to compose more sophisticated and complex temporal forms in their designs. As such it would blur the boundaries between programming and crafting these new smart and computational materials. We envision a material programming practice developed around physical tools (e.g. Fig 1) that draw on bodily skills and experiences (Fig 2) while enabling actions performed directly on the material with immediate effects (no program vs. execution mode). Finally, the tools would enable one layer of abstraction and as such encompass the potential of the computational materials but not that of possibly adjacent computers, which could run more complex algorithms.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Svanæs, Dag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381637"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Interactive Artifacts","Material Programming","Physical Tools","Smart materials","Temporal Forms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material programming a new interaction design practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84978650812","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381637","identifier":[{"id":"84978650812","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-18c8171c-0bc6-4b54-833d-3bd2c500c498"],"keyword":["Interactive Artifacts","Material Programming","Physical Tools","Smart Materials","Temporal Forms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE23E7CF55E7C28ED96546A2DC5E128C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2908805.2909411","eisbn":["9781450343152"],"pages":"149-152","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"DIS '16 Companion","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978650812"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-18c8171c-0bc6-4b54-833d-3bd2c500c498"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Material Programming: A New Interaction Design Practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381637","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we propose the notion of material programming as a future design practice for computational composites. Material programming would be a way for the interaction designer to better explore the dynamic potential of computational materials at hand and through that familiarity be able to compose more sophisticated and complex temporal forms in their designs. The contribution of the paper is an analysis of qualities that we find a material programming practice would and should support: designs grounded in material properties and experiences, embodied programming practice, real-time on-site explorations, and finally a reasonable level of complexity in couplings between input and output. We propose material programming knowing that the technology and materials are not entirely ready to support this practice yet, however, we are certain they will be and that the interaction design community will need to find new ways of relating to such computational materials.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Svanæs, Dag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381695"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Computational Composites","Embodied Programming","Interaction design","Material Programming","Real Time Exploration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material programming a design practice for computational composites","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84997112339","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381695","identifier":[{"id":"84997112339","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1cbaae35-308d-430f-ba74-217578a5f548"],"keyword":["Computational Composites","Embodied Programming","Interaction Design","Material Programming","Real-Time Exploration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9ABE283FD06C86DECF860D87B0DA04E9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2971485.2971554","eisbn":["9781450347631"],"place":"New York, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction (NordiCHI '16)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84997112339"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1cbaae35-308d-430f-ba74-217578a5f548"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Material Programming: a Design Practice for Computational Composites","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381695","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Hardware decays, software obsolesces, infrastructures sediment, devices patinate. While recent scholarship has examined longevity and sustainability, we have little empirical understanding of how things age, decay, and obsolesce and how we might approach impermanence as a resource for practice and reflection. This one-day NordiCHI'16 workshop will bring together researchers from the fields of design, HCI, and anthropology, in order to unpack the temporalities of these forms of impermanence from both theoretical and practical perspectives. The workshop aims to build a rich lexicon for the material and temporal qualities of aging, decay, degradation, and obsolescence by drawing together participants from a broad range of domains working to develop, maintain, or study systems as they age. Drawing together these different perspectives we will consider the various ways that impermanence might serve as a resource for design, use, and maintenance of long-lived technological artifacts.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Cohn, Marisa","Boer, Laurens","Fernaeus, Ylva","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384283"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Aging Technologies","Impermanence in Design","Material Degradation","Obsolescence Studies","Temporalities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"things fall apart unpacking the temporalities of impermanence for hci","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84997470871","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384283","identifier":[{"id":"84997470871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cdee80f4-e354-4cea-8208-ca75d08824bd"],"keyword":["Aging Technologies","Impermanence in Design","Material Degradation","Obsolescence Studies","Temporalities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0BCC285ECE893BAA85ACAF1ADF66162"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ylva","key":"fernaeuspau","last":"Fernaeus","name":"Fernaeus, Ylva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/297148